  "body": "## Problem and behavior\n\nLegacy chat could still expose thread names, previews and message history after a canonical block or consent revocation. This adapter applies the shared PostgreSQL policy to all four existing chat routes, retains current bearer authority in the transaction, and maps known trigger denials to safe HTTP errors. Existing routes and DTOs remain compatible. Missing adapter functions with an installed foundation fail closed.\n\n**Depends on #386** (which depends on #382 and the documented social stack). Draft: the wider social cutover is incomplete. Leave unmerged and undeployed.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Executable DmReads model: 9,648 distinct states; safety and fair read progress passed. Cache, outsider and cursor negative controls produced their specific invariant violations.\n- 1,440 SQL cases generated from checked Read observations passed on private PostgreSQL 16.10. An intentionally unsafe membership-only projection failed at case 36.\n- Actual bearer HTTP/PostgreSQL suite: **93 examples, zero failures**, including 11 new chat cases, revoked-token cases and existing session races.\n- Complete repository-schema fixture: additive apply/reapply and pause preserve messages and denials.\n- Full local Stack build and tests passed: **2,542 examples, zero failures**.\n- Social CI passed at `44a1c7bededf0ba4b54068d482667ac24299f8e4`, including the repaired Docker startup check. Full CI remains separately tracked at its exact SHA.\n\nEvidence and requirement/model/code/test mapping: `docs/social/dm-read-boundary.md`, `docs/social/evidence/dm-read-boundary/`.\n\n## Migration, flags and rollback\n\nApply `2026-09-15_social_v2_chat_api.sql` after the foundation/read-model/DM-write migrations and before this app version serves a database containing the foundation. Additive transaction, three indexes/five functions, no identity rewrite, consent backfill or destructive down migration. Not registered for automatic production migration; index lock duration still needs representative qualification.\n\nKeep social process/UI/database flags inactive. Never-activated legacy participant reads and mutual-follow/admin write semantics remain compatible; canonical policy is retained across pause. Rollback after activation must retain this reader and #386's trigger: disable new UI/work, preserve messages, blocks and activation memory. Old readers must be drained before activation.\n\n## Limits\n\nRead authorization uses the calling statement snapshot; already delivered content is not retracted. Thread lists remain unpaginated, message POST remains non-idempotent, and legacy concurrent writers' ID/commit-order polling gaps remain unqualified. No high-degree latency or conversion uplift claim. Profile/search/media/notifications, delegated entities and native/full-app journeys remain separate work. The handoff retains the earlier automatic-provider deployment exception; no deployment or flag activation is performed by this PR.\n",
